All three functions are implemented and `python3 test_impl.py` prints `ALL PASS` (the stress loop took 13.7s).

- **`encode`** in `rle.py`: each run becomes the character followed by its count, always with a count.
- **`decode`** in `rle.py`: reads a character followed by one or more digits and expands it.
- **`merge`** in `intervals.py`: sorts by start and merges intervals that overlap or touch, returning new lists.

I ran the test after each function as asked; the first two runs failed only on the functions that were still unimplemented. `test_impl.py` is untouched, and nothing is committed.

One limit of the format itself: strings containing digits don't round-trip (`encode("a11")` gives `a112`, which decodes as 112 `a`s). The docstrings don't address it and the tests don't exercise it, so I left it.
